,481,576,2790,10350,882,374,504,220,24,264,744,13,311,220,21,281,744,2572,892,374,220,24,4115,4192,522,37420,91339,29,151645,198,151644,872,198,23526,504,279,74003,13,9258,1172,279,41171,13,3155,537,17024,279,6291,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe owners of the Luray Caverns in Virginia conduct tours every 20 minutes. Each day in April the first tour is at 9 a.m., and the last tour starts at 6 p.m. How many tours are there per day in April?\n\nPartial draft:\n<partial_draft>\nTo determine the number of tours conducted per day at the Luray Caverns in April, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of hours the tours operate each day:**\n   - The first tour starts at 9 a.m.\n   - The last tour starts at 6 p.m.\n   - The total operating time is from 9 a.m. to 6 p.m., which is 9 hours.\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"Continue from the interruption. Output only the continuation. Do not restart the solution.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"69263fdf929584700e2b21328a8a50829bdcb9fbe46f4e81811ec582de68c671"},"seconds":8.045882225036621,"seed":848218633426243484,"stop":"eos","text":"2. **Convert the operating time into minutes:**\n   - Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, 9 hours equals \\(9 \\times 60 = 540\\) minutes.\n\n3. **Calculate the number of tours:**\n   - Tours are conducted every 20 minutes.\n   - The total number of tours is the total operating time in minutes divided by the interval between tours.\n   - Therefore, the number of tours per day is \\(540 \\div 20 = 27\\).\n\nThus, the number of tours per day in April is \\(\\boxed{27}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{27}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":true},"graded_text":"2. **Convert the operating time into minutes:**\n   - Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, 9 hours equals \\(9 \\times 60 = 540\\) minutes.\n\n3. **Calculate the number of tours:**\n   - Tours are conducted every 20 minutes.\n   - The total number of tours is the total operating time in minutes divided by the interval between tours.\n   - Therefore, the number of tours per day is \\(540 \\div 20 = 27\\).\n\nThus, the number of tours per day in April is \\(\\boxed{27}\\).","id":"algebra:932"}
